// The engine↔game contract (L1). The engine DECLARES the seam as a typed
// interface; a game provides the one `implement` block (its manifest,
// games/<game>/config/game.emp) binding each member to a symbol or value. This
// module emits nothing — it is pure declaration. The engine names members
// qualified (`Game.MEMBER`, `#Game.entry`) and calls hooks with
// `invoke Game.hook`, which lowers to an absolute `jsr` when a game binds the
// hook and to ZERO bytes when the hook stays `= empty`.
//
// GameState (the state-dispatch proc type the `entry` member is typed by) is
// `pub type`-declared in engine.game_loop, its dispatch-use home; the bind pass
// resolves member types across the whole reachable module set, so the interface
// consumes it without a cross-module type import (contract types are module-local
// by the import model).
module engine.game_contract

pub interface Game {
    // Comptime feature gate the engine's lowering consumes: the camera's
    // landing-lock arms comptime-select on it (a `CAMERA_JUMP_LOCK = false` game
    // gets the plain deadzone follow).
    const CAMERA_JUMP_LOCK: bool

    // The parallax capability mask (Scanline Services §3): which scanline services
    // ANY scene in this game demands, ORed across the game's whole scene registry.
    // A GAME-level fact by construction — one tier above acts, two above sections —
    // because the P2 lowering has to decide what machinery to OMIT before any section
    // is known, and a per-section value cannot answer that question.
    //
    // Derived-and-verified, never hand-maintained-unchecked: a game's scene registry
    // folds its scenes through fold_caps() (engine/level/scene_dsl.emp) and an ensure
    // there proves the fold is a SUBSET of this declaration. The direction is the
    // safety property — a declared SUPERSET only forgoes a specialisation, while a
    // declared subset would drop machinery a scene still demands.
    //
    // Typed u16 for the end state, not for today's reach: P1 defines five bits up to
    // $0010, and the P3+ bits reserved in scene_dsl.emp reach $0800. Note the width is
    // documentary — sigil's contract checker range-checks no const member, only that
    // the bound value is int-ish — so the registry's ensure is the whole guard.
    //
    // NO ENGINE CONSUMER EXISTS YET. Unlike every other member here, nothing reads
    // `Game.SCANLINE_CAPS`, so it lowers to nothing and moves no ROM byte; it is
    // contract surface that the scene registry can be checked against. The comptime
    // arms that make these bits load-bearing arrive in P2.
    const SCANLINE_CAPS: u16

    // The boot handoff: the first game-state routine and its state id. Boot ends
    // with `move.l #Game.entry, (Game_State).w` + `move.b #Game.ENTRY_ID, ...`.
    const ENTRY_ID: u8
    proc entry: GameState

    // Engine-invoked, game-implemented hooks. `= empty` declares the default —
    // an unbound hook's call site emits NOTHING (empty costs zero bytes, the
    // canonical-shape invariant).
    //
    // boot_hook: engine boot invokes this after Sound_Init, before the game-state
    // handoff. clobbers(d0-d4/a0-a1) is the honest bound: sonic4's
    // SoundTest_BootPing calls Sound_PlayMusic (clobbers d0-d4/a0-a1), whose
    // d2-d4 leak past the ping's own d0/a0 — a generous boot-time bound (every
    // register is free post-boot) that the real impl satisfies exactly.
    hook boot_hook () clobbers(d0-d4/a0-a1) = empty

    // debug_tick: engine GameLoop invokes this once per frame after VSync/SFX
    // drain. ⊤ (d0-d7/a0-a6) — it runs beside the GameState dispatch's own ⊤
    // bound; sonic4's Debug_MusicToggle (clobbers d0-d4/a0-a1) sits inside it.
    hook debug_tick () clobbers(d0-d7/a0-a6) = empty

    // ring_collected: RingCollision (engine/objects/rings.emp) invokes this once per
    // collected ring, AFTER the collect bookkeeping (collected bit, loaded bit,
    // Ring_Counter, SFX) and BEFORE RingBuffer_Remove, with a3 = the ring's buffer
    // entry (X.w at +0, Y.w at +2 — the engine-space centre — then section_id.b,
    // list_index.b; RING_BUFFER_ENTRY_SIZE bytes). The entry is still valid at the
    // call. A game binds its collect visual here (sonic4: RingSparkle_Spawn); the demo
    // leaves it `= empty`. Handing the POINTER rather than loading X/Y into d0/d1 on
    // the engine side keeps the unbound case at exactly zero bytes (the demo ROM is
    // byte-identical with or without the hook). The bound is the spawner's exact need
    // (AllocEffect's d0/a1 + two coords) and deliberately excludes every register
    // RingCollision holds live across the collect path (a2/a3 cursors, d4-d7 player
    // coords and loop counters) — a3 in particular is an INPUT the hook must preserve.
    hook ring_collected (a3: *u8) clobbers(d0-d2/a1) = empty

    // spring_launched: Touch_Spring (engine/objects/collision.emp) invokes this
    // on a TOP contact between a falling player and a COLLISION_SPRING object,
    // AFTER it has seated the player on the spring's top edge and copied the
    // spring's y_vel into him as the launch impulse, with a2 = the player SST and
    // a3 = the spring SST. Both are still valid at the call and neither needs to
    // survive it — TouchResponse's dispatch movem restores a2-a4 either way.
    //
    // WHAT THE ENGINE CANNOT DO ITSELF, which is the whole reason this member
    // exists: the impulse is a velocity, but leaving a grounded player with an
    // upward velocity does nothing — his own ground state re-attaches him next
    // tick. Only the game owns a player state machine, so only the game can put
    // him in the air. A game that places a COLLISION_SPRING object and leaves
    // this `= empty` gets a spring that visibly does nothing; that is a binding
    // error, not an engine one, and it is stated here because nothing can check
    // it (the engine cannot see which collision types a game's level data uses).
    //
    // The bound is the sonic4 impl's exact need — a state value in d0, the
    // player pointer moved into a0 for Player_SetState's a0 slot, and
    // Player_SetState's own d1-d2/a1-a2 — plus the two input registers it is
    // free to consume.
    //
    // `= empty` costs zero bytes AT THE CALL SITE. That is a claim about this
    // MEMBER and it is easy to over-read into "a game without springs pays
    // nothing", which is false and was measured: Touch_Spring's BODY is engine
    // code, so demo carries it whether or not it binds the hook. Measured
    // 2026-09-05 (demo.debug.bin, baseline vs the spring parcel): the collision
    // section grew 116 bytes and every symbol after it shifted by exactly that,
    // while EndOfRom stayed at $1121A — the growth fits the slack before the
    // next fixed anchor, so the ASSEMBLED ROM is the same length and only the
    // deb2 appendix moved (35062 -> 35036 B, tracking the changed symbol names).
    // 116 bytes of a second inlined solid_face_response for a handler demo never
    // dispatches. Cheap, and worth saying out loud rather than leaving a reader
    // to infer zero from the hook's zero.
    hook spring_launched (a2: *u8, a3: *u8) clobbers(d0-d2/a0-a2) = empty

    // solid_pushed: solid_face_response's SIDE arm (engine/objects/collision.emp)
    // invokes this after it has pushed the player out of a solid's left or right
    // face and cleared his x_vel, with a2 = the player SST. It fires ONLY when
    // the player was travelling into the face (the direction gate documented on
    // the template); a player merely standing beside a solid does not reach it,
    // and that distinction is the whole reason this can safely zero a speed.
    //
    // WHAT THE ENGINE CANNOT DO ITSELF, which is the whole reason this member
    // exists, and it is the SAME wall spring_launched leaves through: x_vel is
    // the AIRBORNE driver, but a grounded player is driven by the game's inertia
    // field (sonic4: PlayerV.ground_speed), which his ground state re-derives
    // x_vel from every tick. That field lives in the game's PlayerV overlay of
    // the SST custom window; the engine may not name it, and reaching around the
    // seam by poking a game-owned offset is exactly what the seam exists to
    // prevent. So the engine does the half it owns and hands over the half it
    // does not. A game that leaves this `= empty` gets S3K-correct position and
    // airborne behaviour but keeps its running speed through a side contact
    // (measured before this member existed: rest 10px inside a 17px face while
    // pushing, and 140 frames of friction to settle after release —
    // docs/DEFERRED_WORK.md SP-1).
    //
    // NOT FOLDED INTO spring_launched, and the two are not variants of one hook:
    // that one means "a falling player hit a TOP face and is being thrown", is
    // invoked from one consumer, and its binding runs a state transition; this
    // one means "a moving player hit a SIDE face and is being stopped", is
    // invoked from both consumers' spliced copies of the same template, and its
    // binding is a single store. Sharing a member would force every binding to
    // re-derive which face it was called for from the geometry — which is the
    // per-orientation re-derivation the shared template exists not to reproduce.
    //
    // clobbers() — EMPTY, and that is the honest bound rather than a generous
    // one: sonic4's Solid_Pushed is `clr.w PlayerV.ground_speed(a2)` + `rts` and
    // touches no register at all. It is stated tight on purpose, because the
    // call sits inside a comptime template spliced into Touch_Solid and
    // Touch_Spring and a wider bound would widen BOTH consumers' declared sets.
    // A future binding that needs registers moves this line and both headers
    // with it.
    hook solid_pushed (a2: *u8) clobbers() = empty
}
